Subject: [PATCH 0/3] Add just process-email
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev

This adds `just process-email`, which drains the lab-devel inbox one
message at a time. Each message gets a fresh `claude --permission-mode
auto -p "/process-email <id>"`. The loop runs outside the model:
claude's output goes to /dev/null, and the loop takes its control
signals from notmuch alone. It ends when the inbox is empty. If a pass
leaves its message in the inbox, the loop stops rather than retrying
that message forever.

The query that picks the oldest message now lives in one place,
`just get-oldest-inbox-message`. The loop and the skill both call it.
/process-email takes an optional id argument and falls back to that
recipe when none is given, so running the skill by hand still works.

Testing: I ran the loop with a stub `claude` on PATH against a scratch
copy of the inbox. With a stub that answers nothing, it stops after
the first message with "is still in the inbox" and exits 1. With a
stub that clears the inbox tag, it took all three messages oldest
first and exited 0.

Notes:
- The loop does not fetch. It walks the inbox as currently indexed,
  and the passes themselves fetch new mail. If the local index is
  empty when it starts, it exits without running claude, even when
  upstream holds new mail.
- The recipes use the caller's notmuch config, so run them as the
  agent's user. Pat's config would index a different inbox.
- Two pending patches also edit step 2 of the skill, "[PATCH] claude:
  Treat unintegrated mail as revisable drafts" [1] and "[PATCH]
  claude: Update stale threads from process-email" [2]. Whichever
  lands second will need a small rebase.

